{"ts":"2026-08-05T18:17:35.056Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ac5e22eebf92a6af581282d9","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.222","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-x0iv17"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The one projection that promises completeness is the one that loses data: pm contracts --full drops all 76 structured command summaries, returns 160 bare name strings, and reports has_omissions false"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":""},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","contracts","omission-receipt","projection","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-05T18:17:35.056Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-05T18:17:35.056Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Either --full is a strict superset of the default projection, or its omission receipt names every field group it drops with an accurate restore hint; One key name carries one row shape across every projection of a command; a key does not mean structured records in one projection and bare strings in another; A gate proves, for every command that declares projections, that a projection reporting has_omissions false is field-wise complete against every narrower projection of the same command; The agent-facing cold start keeps working from the declared row_contract without the agent having to discover which projection happens to carry the intent metadata"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A projection that declares has_omissions false carries everything the narrower projections carry, so an agent that follows the receipt's own restore_with hint never loses a field it already had."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm contracts --json returns command_summaries with 76 structured records (command, intent, flags, default_max_estimated_tokens) and an empty commands array, and declares has_omissions true with restore_with --full. Following that hint, pm contracts --full --json returns command_summaries empty and commands as 160 bare strings including subcommand spellings like 'beads import' — the intent, flag and token-budget metadata is gone — while declaring has_omissions false."}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"8239f8e0c946d77307ab0098440f067373782ea1e8ed173ea6372e9fdb42277f","message":"Duplicate check: pm-7i97c3 (contracts intent placeholders), pm-sb0tns (no common row contract across read surfaces), pm-srns (uniform output contract), pm-wv47pf (budget-omitted rows recorded as served) — none covers a completeness-declaring projection that is lossy."}
