{"ts":"2026-08-05T18:18:10.921Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ac5e22eebf92a6af581282d9","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.222","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-05T18:18:10.921Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-05T18:18:10.921Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reproduced 2026-08-05 on this checkout:\n\n  pm contracts --json        -> commands: [] (length 0), command_summaries: 76 records,\n                                omission_receipt.has_omissions = true,\n                                omitted_field_groups = [{name: full_contract_catalog, restore_with: --full}]\n  pm contracts --full --json -> commands: 160 bare strings, command_summaries: 0,\n                                omission_receipt.has_omissions = false\n\nThe declared row_contract does keep an agent honest if it uses the published jq_selector: row_keys is [command_summaries, commands] by default and [commands] under --full, so the selector returns the right rows in both. The defect is not that rows are unreachable — it is that the receipt asserts completeness on the projection that discarded the structured records, and that one key name carries two incompatible row shapes.\n\nThe practical cost for an agent: the default projection is where per-command intent and default_max_estimated_tokens live, and those are exactly the fields an agent needs to budget a call. Reaching for --full to get more loses them, and nothing in the response says so."}]}],"before_hash":"8271f907d5a3badd03ef39e55ebb8340a01f21b51f4e95c4d67d16c649f1704b","after_hash":"ffbf617f151597b4a1550d730d31aa9280379de5de72ef093156d6b18449dc94","message":"Reproduction"}
